!panic: fixedbugs2702acoroutineontheownstackresumedintoahandler001isrefused.answer was called while a signal handler of C's that this runtime saw begin had not been seen to end: either C called it from inside that handler, or C left the handler in a way this runtime does not follow (an inline `__builtin_longjmp`, a C++ exception, a jump inside a system library). A handler not seen to end is held to be running, where neither this runtime's memory nor the C library's is safe to use. No function of the program is a signal handler: after `hero_net_catch_stop() -> i64` (`hero_net.h`), Ctrl-C, SIGTERM and `hero_net_ask_stop() -> ()` only make `hero_net_stop_asked() -> i64` answer 1 and a waiting call of that layer answer stopped; `hero_signal_watch(sig: i32) -> i64` (`hero_os.h`) counts any other signal, and `hero_signal_take(sig: i32) -> i64` gives the count since its last call
